IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aa-estates`

-- Administration Act 1903 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask about an estate, with the seat and the
-- situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (aa-estates.l4) was written from one seat with two faces: the heir or next of kin, and the
-- executor or would-be administrator. Here they are two roles, and two more people the Act gives rights to are added:
--   - a member of the family of someone who has died: the heir's half of the baseline's seat (ss 12A, 13(1a), 14, 15,
--     25(1)(b), 71, 139, Part V, Fourth Schedule);
--   - the executor of a will, or a person who wants to be granted administration: the executor's half (ss 6-8, 25,
--     32, 33, 36, 37, 44, 55, 71, Part V);
--   - a person given something by a will (a beneficiary): s 42 (an order to hand over the gift) and s 143A (interest
--     on a legacy), which the baseline already encodes from that person's seat;
--   - a person owed money by someone who has died (a creditor): s 25(1)(b) (administration to "any other person,
--     whether a creditor or not") and s 37 (administration with the will annexed "upon the application of ... any
--     creditor of the testator").
-- The Court, the Principal Registrar, the Public Trustee as an office and the bank are never seats: what they may or
-- must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when the
-- situation does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the
-- same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. There are three:
--   - `what the person who died left` (`What the person who died left`): no will; a will that leaves some property
--     undisposed of; a will that disposes of all their property. The Act ties s 14 and s 15 to "the property as to which
--     they die intestate" (s 14(1)), so every question of the Table, s 12A, s 13(1a), s 14(4) and the Fourth Schedule
--     does not arise for a will that disposes of everything. s 25 is about "the estate of a person dying intestate", so
--     its three questions arise only for no will. s 71 and s 37 are about a will, so their questions do not arise for
--     no will.
--   - `I am named as executor in the will` (BOOLEAN): ss 32 and 37 are about "an executor"; FALSE, does not arise.
--   - `a grant has been made to me` (BOOLEAN): s 44 follows s 43's duty of "every person to whom probate or
--     administration is granted"; FALSE, does not arise.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (how much is left for the Table, which grant, what a grant
-- vests, s 55, s 139, Part V, and the beneficiary's two) takes no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in aa-estates.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the family member and the executor
-- each answer is the baseline export's own answer, wrapped. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input (the
-- baseline's s 43(1)(b) duty is a DEONTIC and is not asked; s 44, what follows, is).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Administration Act 1903 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a member of the family of someone who has died`
    `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate`
    `I am given something by a will`
    `I am owed money by someone who has died`

-- The situation of the whole estate: whether there is a will, and whether it disposes of everything (s 14(1)).
DECLARE `What the person who died left` IS ONE OF
    `no will`
    `a will that leaves some of their property undisposed of`
    `a will that disposes of all their property`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Fraction` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `a fraction of` HAS `the part` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Rate` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `a yearly rate of` HAS `the yearly rate` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Table item answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the item` IS A `Table item`

DECLARE `Grant answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the grant` IS A `Grant`

DECLARE `Home answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `my right` IS A `My right to take the home`

DECLARE `Registrar answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `what follows` IS A `What s 44 does to me`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation helpers list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes
-- the OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was not read).
GIVEN `what was left` IS A `What the person who died left`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `nothing is left to intestacy` IF
    CONSIDER `what was left`
    WHEN `no will` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will that leaves some of their property undisposed of` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will that disposes of all their property` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `what was left` IS A `What the person who died left`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a will` IF
    CONSIDER `what was left`
    WHEN `no will` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will that leaves some of their property undisposed of` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will that disposes of all their property` THEN TRUE

-- s 25(1)(b), read again (finding QA-1 in NOTES.md): administration may go to "any other person ... if there be no such
-- person entitled as aforesaid resident within the jurisdiction and fit to be so entrusted, or if the person entitled as
-- aforesaid fails, when duly cited, to appear and apply". The baseline's `May an outsider be granted administration`
-- writes this on one line as NOT a OR b, which the stable l4 reads as NOT (a OR b): it answers no when the entitled
-- person was cited and failed to appear. The baseline is not changed (layers are added); this helper bracketing the NOT
-- is what the family member's s 25(1)(b) question uses. It agrees with the baseline whenever no one failed to appear.
GIVEN `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entitled person failed to appear when cited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `someone not entitled may be granted administration` IF
    (NOT (`someone entitled is resident in WA and fit`)) OR `the entitled person failed to appear when cited`

§§ `For a member of the family of someone who has died`

§§§ `s 14(1) -- the intestate property`

@export After the will, how much of my relative's net estate is left to be divided as intestate property (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the net estate` IS A NUMBER @desc The net value of the estate at the date of death, in dollars
      `the value the will disposes of` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the property the will effectively gives away, in dollars (0 if there is no will)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of my relative's estate is left for the Table` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN amount (`How much is left for the Table` `the net estate` `the value the will disposes of`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 14(1) Table, s 15 -- who takes, and how much`

@export Which item of the Table divides my relative's intestate property (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
GIVETH A `Table item answer`
`Which item of the Table divides my relative's property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`Which item of the Table applies` `the family`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my relative's intestate property pass to the Crown by escheat (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1), Table item 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my relative's property pass to the Crown` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does the property pass to the Crown` `the family`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much do I take from my relative's intestate property, for a line the whole line's share (Administration Act 1903 (WA) ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `who I am` IS A `My place in the family` @desc How you were related to the deceased
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
      `the sums` IS A `Legacy sums` @desc The legacy sums in force when the deceased died (the original sums unless a s 14A order applies)
      `the net value` IS A NUMBER @desc Net value of the intestate property at the date of death in dollars, leaving out household chattels where a partner survives
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of my relative's property do I take` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much do I take` `who I am` `the family` `the sums` `the net value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What fraction of my relative's household chattels do I take (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1), Table item 1, with s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `who I am` IS A `My place in the family` @desc How you were related to the deceased
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
GIVETH A `Fraction`
`What fraction of the household chattels do I take` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `a fraction of` (`What share of the household chattels do I take` `who I am` `the family`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my relative's de facto partner take on the intestacy (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my relative's de facto partner take` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does a de facto partner take` `the family`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What fraction of the partner's entitlement goes to my relative's de facto partner (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
GIVETH A `Fraction`
`What fraction goes to my relative's de facto partner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `a fraction of` (`the de facto partner's fraction` `the family`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does anyone take as my relative's partner, a husband, wife or qualifying de facto partner (Administration Act 1903 (WA) ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does anyone take as my relative's partner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does a partner take` `the family`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 14(1) Table, s 14(2b), (3), (3a) -- how the property is divided between the groups`

@export How much of my relative's intestate property goes to the partner side, before any s 15 split (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1), Table items 2-4, s 14(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
      `the sums` IS A `Legacy sums` @desc The legacy sums in force when the deceased died (the original sums unless a s 14A order applies)
      `the net value` IS A NUMBER @desc Net value of the intestate property at the date of death in dollars, leaving out household chattels where a partner survives
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much goes to my relative's partner side` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`the partner's entitlement` `the family` `the sums` `the net value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of my relative's intestate property goes to the issue, children and the issue of dead children, together (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1), Table items 2 and 5, s 14(2b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
      `the sums` IS A `Legacy sums` @desc The legacy sums in force when the deceased died (the original sums unless a s 14A order applies)
      `the net value` IS A NUMBER @desc Net value of the intestate property at the date of death in dollars, leaving out household chattels where a partner survives
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much goes to my relative's issue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`the issue's share` `the family` `the sums` `the net value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of my relative's intestate property goes to the parents together (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1), Table items 3, 6 and 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
      `the sums` IS A `Legacy sums` @desc The legacy sums in force when the deceased died (the original sums unless a s 14A order applies)
      `the net value` IS A NUMBER @desc Net value of the intestate property at the date of death in dollars, leaving out household chattels where a partner survives
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much goes to my relative's parents` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`the parents' share` `the family` `the sums` `the net value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of my relative's intestate property goes to the brothers and sisters, and the children of dead ones, together (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(1), Table items 3, 6 and 8, s 14(3a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
      `the sums` IS A `Legacy sums` @desc The legacy sums in force when the deceased died (the original sums unless a s 14A order applies)
      `the net value` IS A NUMBER @desc Net value of the intestate property at the date of death in dollars, leaving out household chattels where a partner survives
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much goes to my relative's brothers and sisters` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`the brothers' and sisters' share` `the family` `the sums` `the net value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 14(4) -- interest on the partner's statutory legacy`

@export How much interest am I owed on my statutory legacy, 5% a year from the death until it is paid (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 14(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the sum unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the item 2 or item 3 legacy sum still unpaid, in dollars
      `years from the death to payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Years (may be fractional) from the death to payment or appropriation, whichever is earlier
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much interest am I owed on my statutory legacy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much interest am I owed on my legacy` `the sum unpaid` `years from the death to payment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 12A, s 13(1a) -- the relationship, and land held for two or more`

@export Is my parent-child relationship with my relative recognised for the intestacy, if the Court is satisfied of the facts (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 12A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `my parents are or have been married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child's parents are or ever were married to each other
      `established under the Artificial Conception Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relationship was established by the Artificial Conception Act 1985
      `parentage admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parent admitted parentage, or it was established against them, while the parent was alive
      `I am the parent claiming from the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is a parent's claim on a child's estate
      `parentage admitted or established in the child's lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether parentage was admitted or established while the child was alive
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my relationship with my relative recognised` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my relationship recognised` `my parents are or have been married to each other` `established under the Artificial Conception Act` `parentage admitted or established in the parent's lifetime` `I am the parent claiming from the child` `parentage admitted or established in the child's lifetime`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do we who inherit my relative's land on the intestacy hold it as tenants in common (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 13(1a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the persons entitled to the land` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are entitled to the land under ss 14 and 15
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do we hold my relative's land as tenants in common` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Do we hold the land as tenants in common` `the persons entitled to the land`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Fourth Schedule cll 1-3 -- the surviving partner's election to take the home`

@export As the surviving husband, wife or de facto partner, may I elect to take the home towards my share (Administration Act 1903 (WA) Fourth Schedule cll 1-3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `who I am` IS A `My place in the family` @desc How you were related to the deceased
      `the family` IS A `The family left behind` @desc Who survived the deceased
      `the sums` IS A `Legacy sums` @desc The legacy sums in force when the deceased died (the original sums unless a s 14A order applies)
      `the net value` IS A NUMBER @desc Net value of the intestate property at the date of death in dollars, leaving out household chattels where a partner survives
      `the home` IS A `The home` @desc Facts about the house you lived in
GIVETH A `Home answer`
`May I elect to take my relative's home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `nothing is left to intestacy` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`May I elect to take the home` `who I am` `the family` `the sums` `the net value` `the home`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 25(1)(b) -- an outsider as administrator`

@export May someone not entitled to a share, such as the Public Trustee or a creditor, be granted administration of my relative's estate (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 25(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one person entitled to a share lives in Western Australia and is fit to be entrusted
      `the entitled person failed to appear when cited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person entitled was duly cited and failed to appear and apply
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May someone not entitled be granted administration of my relative's estate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `there is a will` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`someone not entitled may be granted administration` `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` `the entitled person failed to appear when cited`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 139 -- a bank deposit paid without a grant`

@export May the bank pay me my relative's deposit without any grant, if the manager is satisfied of my relationship (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 139)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the balance` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum standing to the deceased's credit in the bank or other ADI, in dollars
      `the proclaimed ceiling` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount declared by proclamation (the deposit's note gives $50,000; the Act's text $1,200)
      `a month has passed since the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one month has passed since the death
      `a grant was produced to the bank within the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether probate or administration was produced to the bank within that month
      `notice of a will or an application was given within the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bank was given written notice of a will to be proved or of an intended application for administration within that month
      `my relation` IS A `My relation to the account holder` @desc How you were related to the deceased
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the bank pay me my relative's deposit without a grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        `yes if` (`May the bank pay me without a grant` `the balance` `the proclaimed ceiling` `a month has passed since the death` `a grant was produced to the bank within the month` `notice of a will or an application was given within the month` `my relation`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 71, Part V -- the will in evidence, and no death duty`

@export Can my relative's will be put in evidence in these proceedings before a grant has issued (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 71)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the proceeding` IS A `Proceeding` @desc The kind of proceeding the will is to be used in
      `a grant has issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether probate or administration has already issued
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my relative's will be put in evidence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `there is a will` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is the will admissible in evidence` `the proceeding` `a grant has issued`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my relative's estate pay death or succession duty under this Act (Administration Act 1903 (WA) Part V)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my relative's estate pay death duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a member of the family of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` `Must the estate pay death duty under this Act`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the executor of a will, or a person who wants to be granted administration`

§§§ `ss 6, 7, 25, 33, 36 -- which grant`

@export Which grant must be applied for to deal with the estate in Western Australia: probate, administration with the will annexed, or letters of administration (Administration Act 1903 (WA) ss 6, 7, 25, 33, 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the death` IS A `The death` @desc Whether there is a will and an executor able to act
GIVETH A `Grant answer`
`Which grant must I apply for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN `the answer is` (`Which grant does the estate need` `the death`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6, 8 -- what the grant carries`

@export Does the grant vest this asset of the deceased in me as executor or administrator (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the asset is in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the asset is situated in Western Australia
      `the asset passed outside the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether other law passed it directly to someone at the death (survivorship of a joint owner, a binding super nomination)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the grant vest this asset in me as executor or administrator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN `yes if` (`Does the grant vest this asset in me` `the asset is in Western Australia` `the asset passed outside the estate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 25 -- administration on intestacy`

@export Am I someone the Court may grant administration of the estate to (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 25)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I am entitled in distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you take a share of the estate under s 14 or s 15
      `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one person entitled to a share lives in Western Australia and is fit to be entrusted
      `the entitled person failed to appear when cited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person entitled was duly cited and failed to appear and apply
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be granted administration of the estate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN
        IF `there is a will` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I be granted administration` `my age` `I am entitled in distribution` `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` `the entitled person failed to appear when cited`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 32, 37 -- losing the executor's place`

@export As the executor named in the will, have I lost my right to the executorship (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 32)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am named as executor in the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will names you as an executor
      `I renounced probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you renounced probate of the will
      `I was personally cited and did not appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were personally cited to take probate and did not appear
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I lost my right to the executorship` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN
        IF NOT (`I am named as executor in the will`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Have I lost my right to be executor` `I renounced probate` `I was personally cited and did not appear`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As executor, can the Court now give administration to someone else because I have neither taken out nor renounced probate within 2 months (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am named as executor in the will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will names you as an executor
      `I have obtained or renounced probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already obtained or renounced probate
      `I was under 18 at the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when the testator died
      `whole months since the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the testator died
      `whole months since I turned 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since your 18th birthday (if you were under 18 at the death)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Court give administration to someone else because I delayed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN
        IF NOT (`I am named as executor in the will`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the Court give administration to someone else for my delay` `I have obtained or renounced probate` `I was under 18 at the death` `whole months since the death` `whole months since I turned 18`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 43(1)(b), 44 -- inventory and accounts`

@export Having been granted probate or administration and not filed the inventory and accounts, what must the Principal Registrar now do about it (Administration Act 1903 (WA) ss 43(1)(b), 44)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been made to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether probate or administration of the estate has been granted to you
      `I have filed the inventory and passed the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have filed the inventory and passed the accounts
      `whole months since the period fixed by the rules ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the period the rules allow for filing expired (0 if not yet expired)
GIVETH A `Registrar answer`
`What must the Principal Registrar do about my accounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN
        IF NOT (`a grant has been made to me`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`What happens if I have not filed my accounts` `I have filed the inventory and passed the accounts` `whole months since the period fixed by the rules ended`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 55 -- small estates`

@export May I apply for the grant direct to the Principal Registrar or a district agent, because the estate is not over $10,000 (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 55)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the value of the property` IS A NUMBER @desc Value of all the property the deceased left, in dollars
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply direct to the Principal Registrar for the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN `yes if` (`May I apply direct to the Principal Registrar` `the value of the property`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 71, Part V -- the will in evidence, and no death duty`

@export Can the will be put in evidence in these proceedings before a grant has issued (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 71)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the proceeding` IS A `Proceeding` @desc The kind of proceeding the will is to be used in
      `a grant has issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether probate or administration has already issued
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the will I am to prove be put in evidence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN
        IF `there is a will` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is the will admissible in evidence` `the proceeding` `a grant has issued`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the estate I administer pay death or succession duty under this Act (Administration Act 1903 (WA) Part V)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the estate I administer pay death duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the executor of a will, or want to be granted administration of an estate` THEN `yes if` `Must the estate pay death duty under this Act`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person given something by a will`

§§§ `s 42 -- a gift held back`

@export May I apply to the Court for an order making the executor hand over my gift (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 42)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the executor has probate or is administrator with the will annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person holding the estate has obtained probate or administration with the will annexed
      `I asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked them in writing to transfer, pay or deliver the gift
      `they neglected or refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they neglected or refused to do so after the request
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply for an order for my gift` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am given something by a will` THEN `yes if` (`May I apply for an order to get my gift` `the executor has probate or is administrator with the will annexed` `I asked in writing` `they neglected or refused`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 143A -- interest on a legacy`

@export At what yearly rate is interest on my legacy computed (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 143A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the rate the will or the Court directs` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The yearly rate (as a fraction, e.g. 0.03) directed by the will or a Court, if any
GIVETH A `Rate`
`At what rate is interest on my legacy computed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am given something by a will` THEN `a yearly rate of` (`At what rate is interest on my legacy` `the rate the will or the Court directs`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person owed money by someone who has died`

§§§ `s 25(1)(b) -- administration to a creditor`

@export As a creditor, may I be granted administration of the estate (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 25(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one person entitled to a share lives in Western Australia and is fit to be entrusted
      `the entitled person failed to appear when cited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person entitled was duly cited and failed to appear and apply
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a creditor may I be granted administration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am owed money by someone who has died` THEN
        IF `there is a will` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I be granted administration` `my age` FALSE `someone entitled is resident in WA and fit` `the entitled person failed to appear when cited`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 37 -- administration with the will annexed when the executor delays`

@export As a creditor, may the Court grant me administration with the will annexed because the executor has neither taken out nor renounced probate within 2 months (Administration Act 1903 (WA) s 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the person who died left` IS A `What the person who died left` @desc Whether the person who died left a will, and whether it disposes of all their property
      `the executor has obtained or renounced probate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the executor named in the will has already obtained or renounced probate
      `the executor was under 18 at the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the executor was under 18 when the testator died
      `whole months since the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the testator died
      `whole months since the executor turned 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole months since the executor's 18th birthday (if the executor was under 18 at the death)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a creditor may I be granted administration with the will annexed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am owed money by someone who has died` THEN
        IF `there is a will` `what the person who died left`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the Court give administration to someone else for my delay` `the executor has obtained or renounced probate` `the executor was under 18 at the death` `whole months since the death` `whole months since the executor turned 18`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
